{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out","id":1298245,"title":"Does anyone else wish it was a VtR instead VtM video game coming out?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-20T18:44:47-07:00","id":1298245,"title":"Does anyone else wish it was a VtR instead VtM video game coming out?","content":"I find the CoD more interesting and exciting then WoD, and I think a VtR game would be really cool? Perhaps set in New Orleans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T18:56:35-07:00","id":1298249,"title":"","content":"While I would love the CofD to get the support and promotion it deserves?<br /> <br /> After the V5 mess, I'm kinda happy to let WW and Modiphius get their acts together with the WoD and leave CofD to Onyx Path... even if it means no VtR videogame for now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T18:59:43-07:00","id":1298251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1298249#post1298249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I'm kinda happy to let WW and Modiphius get their acts together with the WoD and leave CofD to Onyx Path... even if it means no VtR videogame for now.</div> </div> </div> </div>This.<br /> <br /> Also, I'll be honest...I never played World of Darkness. I started CofD when it was the 'New World of Darkness', right after Changeling came out. I've played Bloodlines, though, and I'm familiar with the lore of the World of Darkness. I kind of appreciate having that essentially be the 'video game world' whereas my tabletop games are in a different system and setting. It's not really important, but it works for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T19:10:16-07:00","id":1298254,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see VtR taken for a drive through a generational play experience of personal management and events. Kinda like a mashup of Crusader Kings and The Guild--by night. <br /> <br /> The risk is that you end up with a metagame influencing things. VtR, however, might fare better in that it has some characters and a few defined events, but no meta to speak of. Just sandbox and go.<br /> <br /> There is, however, a fascination with first-person games and at that point you can just write your own factions, mechanics and story to go with the vampire tale you want to tell through the medium. No need to borrow an IP. <br /> <br /> --Khanwulf","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12493-khanwulf","name":"Khanwulf","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12493_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"898"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-20T20:31:32-07:00","id":1298265,"title":"","content":"I would love a Requiem game...so long as I also trusted the job would actually be done by the people it was given to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T07:37:53-07:00","id":1298322,"title":"","content":"I would also love a good Requiem video game, especially because it would make it a lot easier to lead people into Requiem tabletop. At the moment most people know Masquerade from <i>Bloodlines</i>, but Requiem isn't in the cultural consciousness the same way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-21T12:32:10-07:00","id":1298381,"title":"","content":"Requiem has so much more potential just because it is completely open ended with no intricate meta-plot as canon. That being said, I would agree with others here that I would prefer to see it done right, than rushed out just to get a new, shallow Vampire game on the shelves.<br /> Many are setting their expectations on the moon, where were left after Bloodlines and Redemption but I for one expect disappointment in this recreation. I'll still buy it to show my support and give it a fair shake but I hope the NEXT game is VTR done right <i>by night</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T10:19:33-07:00","id":1298979,"title":"","content":"Not really, Requiem would not work in the same way as masquerade does, the lack of established characters and a meta plot is kind of in the way for requiem as an fps-rpg","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25195-evilhamster","name":"Evilhamster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T10:58:05-07:00","id":1298991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evilhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1298979#post1298979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, Requiem would not work in the same way as masquerade does, the lack of established characters and a meta plot is kind of in the way for requiem as an fps-rpg</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. I think it's the opposite- the lack of a metaplot and the open-endedness of Requiem makes it more easy to create a standalone game, not less.<br /> <br /> I actually had been thinking about this long before Bloodlines 2 was announced, about how VtR could inspire a similar game. I feel like it it works pretty well- you have the five clans as ready-made &quot;classes&quot; for the player to choose from. Daeva mixes social skills with physical, Gangrel is all about combat, Mekhet is the stealth option, Nosferatu gives you plenty of crowd control, and Ventrue lets you just Dominate your way through.<br /> <br /> The Covenants are the post-start factions the player can join. Perhaps the city is currently balanced between two factions- the Invictus and Sanctum on once side and an uneasy alliance between the Carthians and Crones on the other. The Ordo Dracul is nominally uninterested... You basically get to choose which one you support, and that changes how the game plays out. (different outcomes, getting First Estate goons supporting you versus Crone witches.)<br /> <br /> The main plot is about the Strix infiltrating the city, and how they are orchestrating things to cause chaos... such as killing the Prince and creating a power vacuum. The player (as a newly-embraced neonate) is one of the few vampires that can be &quot;trusted&quot; not to have committed the murder, since they have a rock-solid alibi- they were dead and buried at the time. (posthumous embrace, natch)<br /> <br /> Throw in some fun gameplay and exploration, and I think it would be pretty interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12970-gellydog","name":"Gellydog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12970_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:53:54-07:00","id":1299006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1298991#post1298991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main plot is about the Strix infiltrating the city, and how they are orchestrating things to cause chaos... such as killing the Prince and creating a power vacuum. The player (as a newly-embraced neonate) is one of the few vampires that can be &quot;trusted&quot; not to have committed the murder, since they have a rock-solid alibi- they were dead and buried at the time. (posthumous embrace, natch)</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of course, you can trust that the corpse didn't do anything\u2026 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T11:54:28-07:00","id":1299008,"title":"","content":"I dig Requiem (the second edition book managed to actually get me interested in a Vampire game when I felt like it wasn't my thing), but maybe the best way to go with a hypothetical CoD videogame might be not to go with Requiem but with another unexpected gameline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-23T12:15:59-07:00","id":1299012,"title":"","content":"I think there's some potential there. Lost 1e was a big turning point in the CofD when it really started to pull away from the WoD and become it's own thing that felt different; and has some strong positive feelings as a game (even if the Underhill thing might have tamped that down) to call on. Court Goodwill can also help explore lots of faction based questlines more easily even Court selection could be significant enough to have replay value.<br /> <br /> While not the most popular games, Promethean and Beast also have a few things that would make them easier to transition to videogames. The both share a setups that are a bit more solo-play friendly, and both have strong 'end game' goals to orient a videogame towards. Different ways of achieving the New Dawn, or becoming an Inheritance predispose a CRPG conversion to more natural multiple choice endings<br /> <br /> Though I'd imagine the familiarity of vampires (or werewolves) as a draw to a more general audience might be a big consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T02:34:00-07:00","id":1299155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299008#post1299008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> maybe the best way to go with a hypothetical CoD videogame might be not to go with Requiem but with another unexpected gameline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree here. As much as I love Requiem and been musing sometimes about a video game for it, I think the best way for CofD to reach some recognition of its own is ignoring the obvious games like VtR (seriously how many games about vampires are out there now?) and use something new and fresh. My vote is for Changeling because fairies are a criminally underrated supernatural creature and deserve more love.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T05:51:55-07:00","id":1299184,"title":"","content":"What a tutorial that would be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:50:49-07:00","id":1299210,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gellydog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1298991#post1298991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree. I think it's the opposite- the lack of a metaplot and the open-endedness of Requiem makes it more easy to create a standalone game, not less.<br /> <br /> I actually had been thinking about this long before Bloodlines 2 was announced, about how VtR could inspire a similar game. I feel like it it works pretty well- you have the five clans as ready-made &amp;quot;classes&amp;quot; for the player to choose from. Daeva mixes social skills with physical, Gangrel is all about combat, Mekhet is the stealth option, Nosferatu gives you plenty of crowd control, and Ventrue lets you just Dominate your way through.<br /> <br /> The Covenants are the post-start factions the player can join. Perhaps the city is currently balanced between two factions- the Invictus and Sanctum on once side and an uneasy alliance between the Carthians and Crones on the other. The Ordo Dracul is nominally uninterested... You basically get to choose which one you support, and that changes how the game plays out. (different outcomes, getting First Estate goons supporting you versus Crone witches.)<br /> <br /> The main plot is about the Strix infiltrating the city, and how they are orchestrating things to cause chaos... such as killing the Prince and creating a power vacuum. The player (as a newly-embraced neonate) is one of the few vampires that can be &amp;quot;trusted&amp;quot; not to have committed the murder, since they have a rock-solid alibi- they were dead and buried at the time. (posthumous embrace, natch)<br /> <br /> Throw in some fun gameplay and exploration, and I think it would be pretty interesting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there could be a game in the future but not in the same way bloodlines is built.<br /> <br /> The CK2 Mod that uses the chronicles of darkness setting is doing a fantastic job, Requiem is another kind of beast then Masqurade...And I meen that in a really good way","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25195-evilhamster","name":"Evilhamster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T07:52:01-07:00","id":1299211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shawarbaaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299155#post1299155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree here. As much as I love Requiem and been musing sometimes about a video game for it, I think the best way for CofD to reach some recognition of its own is ignoring the obvious games like VtR (seriously how many games about vampires are out there now?) and use something new and fresh. My vote is for Changeling because fairies are a criminally underrated supernatural creature and deserve more love.</div> </div> </div> </div> Changeling, Protean or Mage would be awsome to see in a videogame form","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25195-evilhamster","name":"Evilhamster","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T09:21:19-07:00","id":1299240,"title":"","content":"Protean? like just seeing the ability in action?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T10:24:50-07:00","id":1299264,"title":"","content":"Probably meant Promethean.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T11:08:53-07:00","id":1299279,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure the words, &quot;Creative Thaumaturgy&quot; have killed any thoughts of a Mage videogame with our current computing tech.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:41:40-07:00","id":1299324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299279#post1299279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm pretty sure the words, &quot;Creative Thaumaturgy&quot; have killed any thoughts of a Mage videogame with our current computing tech.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeaaaa. -_-<br /> <br /> And it'd be for both Mage games: while Ascension and Awakening have their differences, the principles behind their own takes on freeform spellcasting pose a problem when it comes to translating it to video games. Set limits have to be in place for video games, versus the open-ended creativity in TRPGs.<br /> <br /> Since right off the bat, in a theoretical Awakening game, fans of the TRPG would be making complaints of &quot;Why am I being pigeon-holed into using Fate to progress here when I could easily use Mind instead?&quot; or other such stuff of that nature.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T12:41:47-07:00","id":1299325,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I don't think we'll ever get to the level of Creative Thaumaturgy in a computer game. Demon would work better, but would also be kinda tough to pull off, I think.<br /> <br /> Promethean or Changeling, on the other hand, I'd totally dig. Hunter, too, of course, especially low-tier (no conspiracies), would make for an awesome horror game.<br /> I think Mummy could also be immensely fun, and would fit very well into a PC game format.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest, I'm totally stoked about it being a Masquerade game. Requiem has pretty much replaced V:tM for me, but that doesn't mean I dislike it in any way; it (and Bloodlines especially) always kept a special place in my heart, and I am happy to see it get some love.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T13:13:07-07:00","id":1299355,"title":"","content":"The only way to do those kind of creative systems is by removing them. Think something like the episodic Telltale games. You'd get to choose between a few spells at certain points limited by the predefined character and what makes sense for the situation. You'd be pigeon holed into using certain Arcana because your character only has access to those, not because of the limitations of the medium.<br /> <br /> I can see such games be made really well, but most people who are into the source material will likely not appreciate such constraints even if it's based on the character instead of limited programming space. Especially since it'd remove many other things from an RPG like character creation, character sheets, and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:10:18-07:00","id":1299385,"title":"","content":"If you asked me this question in 2004, I would have answered yes.<br /> <br /> But now in 2019? Nah.<br /> <br /> Vampire the Requiem is amazing, but seeing what is going on with Vampire the Masquerade V5 and what's already going on with Vampire the Masquerade - Bloodlines 2, I'm glad that Vampire the Requiem is in better hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:12:41-07:00","id":1299386,"title":"","content":"that's the thing about tabletop into video games. not every one is call of cthulhu quality (and there's the fact you arent a monster in those games)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T14:52:23-07:00","id":1299410,"title":"","content":"I think there is a way to do Mage... but I'm not sure fans would dig it:<br /> <br /> Rotes with predetermined spell factors only.<br /> <br /> There are videogames that have done custom spell design in-game. It's never going to be the full creativity of Mage, but you can at least have a bunch of spells you made yourself based on your character's stats.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-24T16:20:53-07:00","id":1299450,"title":"","content":"I'm quite pleased that they're making a V5 game. It's set in Seattle, which as I recall, is a <i>really</i> interesting place in CofD, but not so much from the vampires' angle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T01:55:25-07:00","id":1299546,"title":"","content":"Besides Lost, I think Forsaken would be completely bonkers as a game if done right, and kind of scary. Like a trippier version of Princess Mononoke.<br /> <br /> Also something that I would appreciate in a CoD videogame is some sort of visual differentiation. I'm not necesarily a fan of the need for hyper-fotorreal graphics. What if a Lost or Forsaken game were more stylized? What if it looked more less like the illustrations in both editions of Lost? (I like those). And give the artists free reign for leaning into the weird instead of worrying about the hyperrealistic sweat on a character's face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25136,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","user":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","date":". 03-25-2019, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25136-kev\u00e4\u00e4n-neito","name":"Kev\u00e4\u00e4n Neito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25136_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:03:50-07:00","id":1299758,"title":"","content":"I would absolutely adore a Requiem game, or even an Awakened game (it'd be difficult but I think a different kind of game genre would be needed rather than an RPG Stat-based thing like Bloodlines is, not sure how, but there's gotta be a different genre to make it work).<br /> <br /> That said, I wouldn't really say &quot;I'd rather have Requiem than Masquerade&quot;. While I really REALLY want to see CofD get more love and acknowledgement and it would be awesome to see a game based on it, I'm also not sad that Bloodlines is getting a sequel (spiritual or otherwise). <br /> <br /> <br /> I guess I'm not sad that I'm getting Bloodlines 2, I'll play the hell out of it. But I am a little sad that I don't have a CofD equivalent to share with my friends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:20:10-07:00","id":1299762,"title":"","content":"I'd much rather a Vampire the Requiem T.V. series that is done well and is well written. Just my opinion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25183-reslin","name":"Reslin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T16:48:55-07:00","id":1299773,"title":"","content":"A TV show would be cool. On the subject of computer games I think a CofD point and click like Unavowed would be nice, if we're going Vampire then I would look at the Hitman games as a starting point and work out from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T17:37:32-07:00","id":1299792,"title":"","content":"As much as I like games some novels would be cool. I've enjoyed the existing ones for Requiem and the anthologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T19:08:54-07:00","id":1299814,"title":"","content":"Honestly the way I'd make a Requiem game is: Exotic setting with a socio-political background that differentiate it from Masquerade. 5 premade player characters, with their own personalities and ambitions, one from each clan. A plot that involve factional conflict between the different covenants with a finale that involves the Strix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T19:09:48-07:00","id":1299815,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299792#post1299792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As much as I like games some novels would be cool. I've enjoyed the existing ones for Requiem and the anthologies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same here, another full length novel or comic for Requiem would be amazing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12561-shawarbaaz","name":"Shawarbaaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-25T20:15:37-07:00","id":1299827,"title":"","content":"I have literally never played Masquerade or Bloodlines... but people love both, so far be it for me to begrudge them their sequal. <br /> <br /> Although I STILL want a Mummy the Curse video game that is a spiritual successor to Planescape Torment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T08:46:11-07:00","id":1299972,"title":"","content":"I too wish they made more VTR novels and books in story form and I would devour them.<br /> RPG's are great but when I read the existing novels I found myself thinking &quot;What would my character do in this situation?&quot; and that just made it even more enjoyable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11661-rathamus","name":"Rathamus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11661_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:35:42-07:00","id":1299997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathamus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299972#post1299972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I too wish they made more VTR novels and books in story form and I would devour them.<br /> RPG's are great but when I read the existing novels I found myself thinking &quot;What would my character do in this situation?&quot; and that just made it even more enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I agree with this as well. So I'd add &quot;Books or T.V. Series&quot; for me it's the same with a t.v. series too. &quot;What would my character do when confronted with ____?&quot; plus no other Vampire media really compares to the game. The idea of there being different types of vampires with their own innate abilities is unheard of in vampire media.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25183-reslin","name":"Reslin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25183_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:47:06-07:00","id":1300000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1299827#post1299827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although I STILL want a Mummy the Curse video game that is a spiritual successor to Planescape Torment.</div> </div> </div> </div>...versus the actual spiritual successor, Torment: Tides of Numenera? :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T10:56:24-07:00","id":1300002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300000#post1300000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...versus the actual spiritual successor, Torment: Tides of Numenera? :P</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I know, but you know a game with Torment's memory games would be perfect for Mummy XP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T11:03:20-07:00","id":1300003,"title":"","content":"Bloodlines one was awesome, looking forward to the second even if I find myself more at home in the CoD now.<br /> <br /> I do wish it the best, since its success would have consequences on White Wolf/Onyx Path as a whole. And, who knows? Perhaps we'll get CoD games someday.<br /> <br /> My ideal one would be a Telltale style Promethean game, with scenes and consequences that determine the end of the Pilgrimage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-26T12:36:07-07:00","id":1300036,"title":"","content":"Well, I'd say that given how we'll get a new Bloodlines game, maybe some enterprizing individual with more talent than me would take on the project of remaking the game into a VtR version? That would mostly entail changing the Clans to VtR Clans and also re-write much of the dialogue.<br /> <br /> For example in the old Bloodlines the Camarilla (minus the Tremere) becomes the Invictus, Strauss becomes Ordo Dracul, the Sabbat becomes Belial's Brood and the Kuei-Jin either becomes one of the many versions for Asian Covenants that's been suggested across the years or just stay Kuei-Jin and so on.<br /> <br /> Given the awesome work done on the fairly recent WW2 and Clan Quest mods and the unofficial patches for Bloodlines, I think that it should be possible to bring Bloodlines to Requiem, even if you'd to abandon full voice acting for many dialoge lines and lip sync and such.<br /> <br /> And some more exposure for VtR could also be helpful in making the game more known and not just have VtM claim the spotlight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T16:06:54-07:00","id":1300408,"title":"","content":"There's a fantastic Actual Play on these forums that does that for a tabletop playthrough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2291-gwyn-chan-r-gwyll","name":"Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T16:17:29-07:00","id":1300409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300003#post1300003\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines one was awesome, looking forward to the second even if I find myself more at home in the CoD now.<br /> <br /> I do wish it the best, since its success would have consequences on White Wolf/Onyx Path as a whole. And, who knows? Perhaps we'll get CoD games someday.<br /> <br /> My ideal one would be a Telltale style Promethean game, with scenes and consequences that determine the end of the Pilgrimage</div> </div> </div> </div>a telltale style promethean would be amazing. like your choices could influence your next refinement and role and such. with the new dawn success depending on how you've down<br /> <br /> EDIT: Ok, that was off topic. anyway, as much as I would love a chronicles of darkness game, I'll be glad if this bloodlines is good either way (I'm also looking forward to werewolf the apocalypse earthblood). one thing to note about old world of darkness is its meta-plot, which makes it easier to make a game adaptation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24173,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","user":"Primordial newcomer","date":". 03-27-2019, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T16:21:27-07:00","id":1300412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300409#post1300409\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> a telltale style promethean would be amazing. like your choices could influence your next refinement and role and such. with the new dawn success depending on how you've down</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much my idea. Decide which friend to help where either one falls prey to Pandorans or another one feels betrayed and goes Centimanus (only to come back later), make your decisions and determine if New Dawn happens or not. That sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> Not too long, still able to impression players and provide a contained arc which serves Promethean well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 03-27-2019, 07:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T16:56:40-07:00","id":1300419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300412#post1300412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, pretty much my idea. Decide which friend to help where either one falls prey to Pandorans or another one feels betrayed and goes Centimanus (only to come back later), make your decisions and determine if New Dawn happens or not. That sort of stuff.<br /> <br /> Not too long, still able to impression players and provide a contained arc which serves Promethean well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to try to stay on topic with this response this time.<br /> <br /> when you mentioned aspects such as &quot;goes centimanus but then comes back&quot;, I got reminded that before telltale disbanded (and now a new studio composed of the original devs and more has come into being. funny how easy it seems to do that), they claimed they were making a new engine to allow more room for influencing the story. games like the chronicles of darkness could greatly benefit from such games being made (of course, some games do appear to be capable on other kinds of games, as bloodlines more than proved)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-27T23:23:38-07:00","id":1300477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gwyn chan 'r Gwyll</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300408#post1300408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a fantastic Actual Play on these forums that does that for a tabletop playthrough.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know, I've got the PDFs on my computer. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But the &quot;problem&quot; is that this is preaching to the faithful. Those reading that Let's Play will already be fans of VtR. A mod of the computer game would, in my opinion, have a greater chance to reach out and present VtR to those who are not already fans, or even know of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/970-gurkhal","name":"Gurkhal","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"863"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T08:14:33-07:00","id":1300553,"title":"","content":"maybe focusing on a Coterie building a smnall barony in the city?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T11:21:46-07:00","id":1300620,"title":"","content":"Even through the rose-colored lenses of nostalgia, I find so much of the OG World of Darkness material to be childish, even cringe-worthy. When nWoD/CoD first rolled out it felt like the writing staff had grown up, and then re-imagined the core themes of the new game-lines from an adult's perspective. Every singe CoD game is orders of magnitude better than the crude, adolescent scribblings of what came before. I would love for the CoD games to get a big budget video game treatment, but I really don't have much interest in anything based on the oWoD material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2587-zen_hydra","name":"Zen_Hydra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2587_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:32:15-07:00","id":1300635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zen_Hydra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1298245-does-anyone-else-wish-it-was-a-vtr-instead-vtm-video-game-coming-out?p=1300620#post1300620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even through the rose-colored lenses of nostalgia, I find so much of the OG World of Darkness material to be childish, even cringe-worthy. When nWoD/CoD first rolled out it felt like the writing staff had grown up, and then re-imagined the core themes of the new game-lines from an adult's perspective. Every singe CoD game is orders of magnitude better than the crude, adolescent scribblings of what came before. I would love for the CoD games to get a big budget video game treatment, but I really don't have much interest in anything based on the oWoD material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not that I necessarily disagree (nor necessarily agree, I do think CofD is more mature, but I don't think WoD is childish), but could you elaborate and explain what exactly you think is childish about oWoD? Perhaps give a few examples?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24044-ventrue-life","name":"Ventrue Life","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24044_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-28T12:47:28-07:00","id":1300640,"title":"","content":"I'm not entirely sure this is where we would want to take the discussion for this thread. I've seen too many threads get derailed into arguments on the merits of cWoD vs CofD.<br /> <br /> That said, I do think that VtM and VtR scratch two different itches that would necessarily mean that they work in different ways when translated to a VG. VtM works really well with games like Bloodlines, it has NPCs that have large roles and and a kind of fishbowl experience that it is fun to explore.<br /> <br /> VtR on the other hand, I would like a VtR game to focus on the tricksy turning of the Danse Macabre. Something more akin to Vampyr combined with Persona (I'm not super confident in that combo, but you get what I mean, I'd want the medium to highlight VtR's strengths in the same way that Bloodlines highlights VtM's strengths).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}